  "blurb2": "He won five championships with the Minneapolis Lakers across the late forties and early fifties, establishing the franchise's winning identity decades before it ever moved to Los Angeles. Mikan basically proved that a genuinely dominant big man could single-handedly carry a team to sustained success, a lesson that every era since has had to reckon with in one way or another.",
